# Minimum capable model

Re-evaluate on every user message, including follow-ups. You cannot change the
picker; the user must.

Default to the lightest capable tier. Prefer the simplest model that can
complete the task reliably.

| Tier | Use when |
| --- | --- |
| Light | Single-file or obvious fixes, config/docs, simple CRUD, rename/move, cleanup, Q&A |
| Mid | Multi-file work, non-trivial debug, unfamiliar code, cross-module refactors, API/integration |
| Heavy | Architecture, high-risk production, deep unclear bugs, security-critical correctness |

Never pick the heaviest tier because it is available. Never stay on a weaker
model when correctness is at risk.

When the selected model is heavier than recommended, stop and ask the user
whether to switch before implementing or exploring.
